codex
Two findings affect the cost ranking: the PCC2 precedent preserves reads that were already served from backing storage, whereas these six RE read arms serve nothing. Also, TEX’s write index advances by one halfword per eight-byte slot while each write stores four halfwords, so a readback design needs to resolve that overlap. The LINEAR read arms look cheapest to implement, but their current rows still need value-based success expectations.
